> crosswalk@0.7.0 test:adversarial
> tsx scripts/test-adversarial.ts

  ✓ a bare user id is not a session; only the signed cookie value is
  ✓ money arithmetic is exact where floats are not
  ✓ waterfall: contracts beginning today apply, contracts ending today apply, tomorrow's and yesterday's do not; ties choose the lowest price and say so
  ✓ waterfall: a EUR contract never prices a USD question; an unapproved entry never applies
  ✓ recommendation never goes below floor, never above reference; missing cost → no floor, margin unknown, not zero
  ✓ competitor intelligence: an absurd observation (case price as unit price) does not become KNOWN_ACCOUNT on its own
  ✓ submit routes the three lines correctly and locks the proposal
  ✓ CHAIN: changes-requested on one line must not let a repriced sibling line be approved against a stale snapshot
  ✓ CHAIN: resubmission after changes-requested supersedes old requests; the proposal can still reach APPROVED
  ✓ exported quote carries exactly the approved prices; nothing mutated after approval
  ✓ a rep cannot export before approval, a clinical reviewer cannot export at all, finance cannot set prices
  ✓ two managers deciding the same request simultaneously: exactly one decision is recorded
  ✓ double submit in parallel creates one set of approval requests
  ✓ parallel price edits on one line leave a consistent line and one audit event per write
  ✓ negative, zero, NaN and absurd prices are refused; a 100% discount needs the committee
  ✓ a won proposal's contract cannot be deleted from under it; a request with proposals cannot be deleted
  ✓ intake parser survives formulas, unicode, huge quantities, blanks and duplicate headers; CSV output neutralises formula injection
  ✓ cost, floor and margin never reach a rep through the audit trail or nested recommendation JSON
  ✓ a cross cannot be approved on one signature, with no equivalence, or with an invented status
  ✓ purchase and cost imports are idempotent and skip bad rows with a reason
  ✓ a policy that would disable floors or invert authority is refused; a sane draft is accepted
  ✓ renaming the company keeps the catalog (no second Company row); bad settings are refused
  ✓ a rep-proposed cross must name a real SKU and a real match type
  ✓ an approved proposal past its valid-through date cannot be exported

